why: stage 0 landed (c2ff5cfe); the Schema is an optic algebra that has
  not been named, and Form.edit routes dotted string paths over Json by
  hand. The second-order drift law — the value optic and the Json optic
  commute with the codec — is the part of this arc only a library with
  both can state.

what: okay-codec's Json optics (`at` as the Option lens, `field`/`index`/
  `caseOf` as affines over it, `values`/`entries` as traversals), the
  dotted path from a Schema, and the commuting law on a type with
  nesting, a sum and a list. Whether Form.edit is REWRITTEN on them is
  decided by what the code says: its `editAt` also creates missing
  parents and interprets Add/Del/Choose, which may not be the
  composition of lawful optics — if it is not, the finding is recorded
  and Form keeps its router, with a test asserting the two agree where
  they overlap.

predict: `at` is the lawful one (Option in the focus) and `field` is
  derived from it — the lens/at-ix pair; the law is a few lines and the
  work is the sum and list shapes.
